{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel came into the midst of the sea.</b> The children of Israel did not cross the sea along its width, for it is known that the sea does not separate between the land of Egypt and the land of Canaan. Rather, they did not need to enter it except so that Pharaoh would enter after them and drown. And they entered it in a semicircle, for from the wilderness of Etham they entered the sea, and from the wilderness of Etham they returned from the sea." "<b>Into the midst of the sea.</b> Even if they entered it only half a parsang, it is called 'within,' as it is written: 'and the mixed multitude that was בקרבו' — and they were not in the middle of the camp."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:49.547321283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}